# TT.TICKET_INTERFACE -- merge_tickets (S-TICKET-034..036: events re-pointed with
# org_ticket_id, duplicate notifications deleted and the rest moved, change requests and
# suppressed signatures moved, ratings merged by GREATEST id, partner reference adopted,
# fast_resolvable poisoned, newer last public event wins, source -> status 110 with
# close/resolve dates, target -> status 3 with the hot reason; both STRICT ticket lookups
# propagate NO_DATA_FOUND) and deleteTicket (S-TICKET-052: the 31-statement cascade across
# tt, fw, guma2, mc, mcaudit, mss, nids and prx -- every dependent row of ticket 954325 is
# removed or de-referenced; a nonexistent ticket is a silent no-op).
#
# ORA_USER=system: the fixtures insert into stop.*, mss.*, auth.login, mc.*, mcaudit.*,
# prx.*, nids.*, fw.* and guma2.*; TT holds no DML privilege on most of those. Everything
# is rolled back at the end (COMMITS=no).
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=merge_tickets 954320->954321 and 954323->954322 plus NO_DATA_FOUND paths; deleteTicket 954325 with a dependent row in every cascaded table
